WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Do you know that at the time of Rasulullah sallallahu alaihi wa sallam, what were the Jews doing in Medina?

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.500
Has anyone asked themselves this question? How did they come to Medina?

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.000
They came to Medina because in the Tawrah and the Tilmood that the Jews believe in,

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.500
there was description of the land in which the final messenger would come.

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:27.000
And this final messenger was mentioned in the Tawrah and the description was that this place would have date palms.

6
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:33.000
And there were several other descriptions which fitted precisely to Medina to Munawara

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
and that is why they all flocked to Medina to Munawara.

8
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
From amongst them were their leaders and the general public and so on.

9
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
One day when Rasulullah sallallahu alaihi wa sallam made hijrah from Makkah to Medina,

10
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Abdullah ibn Salam who happened to be one of the Jewish leaders,

11
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.000
he was working in a farm of his around Medina and he noticed the cloud moving.

12
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
He noticed a group of people moving and he noticed so many other signs. He was a rabbi.

13
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
He noticed so many signs. He said, no, today is the day. We have all been waiting for so long.

14
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Today is the day that this prophet is going to come.

15
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:17.000
So he left his work and he went towards this cloud of people who were blocking his view.

16
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.000
He wanted to see the face of Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam

17
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
and he knew as soon as I see the face I am going to recognize whether he is a prophet or not

18
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.000
because he had seen all the other signs. The cloud was covering wherever he was and so on.

19
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
So then he came and he had a peep at Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam

20
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.000
and immediately he declared this is the prophet of Allah.

21
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
I bear witness that you are the prophet that we are waiting for. Subhanallah.

22
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.000
So all the people around began to say Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar.

23
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Do you know that this is the leader of the Jews? He is accepting Islam.

24
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:57.000
He has come here and he is declaring that you are a messenger and he is going to the description of the Torah.

25
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.000
So Rasulullah sallallahu alaihi wa sallam called him and said, Ya Abdullah, Abdullah ibn Salam, come here.

26
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.000
You are one of the leaders of the Jews.

27
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Why don't you go to the Jews and inform them that the messenger has arrived?

28
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.000
So he said, Ya Rasulullah, I know my people. They will turn away.

29
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.000
They will not listen even to me when it comes to their desires.

30
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.000
I hope the Muslim Ummah is not doing this today

31
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.000
that when it comes to their desires we are not interested in what is right and wrong anymore.

32
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.000
Abdullah ibn Salam mentioned that this was a quality of his own people.

33
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.000
So Rasulullah sallallahu alaihi wa sallam said, No, try with them at least.

34
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.000
So Rasulullah sallallahu alaihi wa sallam made Abdullah ibn Salam go behind the wall

35
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.000
and the Jews were called of Medina and he asked them, Who is Abdullah ibn Salam?

36
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.000
They said he is our leader and the son of our leader.

37
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.000
He is the most honest from amongst us and the son of the most honest.

38
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.000
He is one of our champions and the son of the champion. He is a brother and the son of a brother.

39
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:58.000
So Rasulullah sallallahu alaihi wa sallam said, What if I were to tell you that he accepted me as a prophet?

40
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.000
They said that is impossible. We don't even want to discuss that because it cannot happen.

41
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:09.000
So Abdullah ibn Salam emerged from the back and said, In me, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.

42
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.000
I bear witness that Muhammad, his servant and his messenger.

43
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Immediately all the congregations who were there from amongst his people

44
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.000
began to say he is the liar and his father was a liar. He is a cheater and his father was a cheater.

45
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.000
He is the worst and his father was the worst.

46
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.000
And Abdullah ibn Salam looked at Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam and told him, Do you know?

47
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Didn't I tell you? I know my people better than anyone else. So then what had happened?

48
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:38.000
Banu Quraida and Banu Nadeer. These are the two clans of the Jews whom Abdullah ibn Salam had belonged to.

49
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.000
They did not talk to Abdullah ibn Salam and the few who had accepted Islam with him.

50
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.000
They didn't want to sit with them. They didn't want to associate with them.

51
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.000
There was no intermarriage even between their children or even themselves.

52
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Absolutely no form of communication between them and their own people.

53
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.000
So this used to touch them in their hearts. So they came to Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam

54
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.000
and complained. Abdullah ibn Salam himself said, Oh Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam,

55
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.000
ever since we have accepted Islam, these people don't talk to us. They don't want to associate with us.

56
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.000
They don't want to sit with us. They don't want us to intermarry in any way whatsoever.

57
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:19.000
And we don't have any friends now. Jibril alaihi wa sallam came down with verses.

58
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:46.000
Abdullah ibn Salam and the group don't worry at all. Don't worry that you don't have friends.

59
00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:53.000
Your friend is Allah. Your friend is Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam. Your friends are all the believers.

60
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:59.000
Those who establish Salah and those who give zakah whilst they are in huku and subhanallah.

61
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:05.000
He was so comforted with this and he always used to say subhanallah, Allah has befriended me.

62
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:10.000
Allah has befriended me. I complained. I didn't have friends. What happens to us today?

63
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.000
We decide to become a little bit religious. Sometimes a person becomes slightly religious.

64
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Some of his own or her own family members excommunicate them. Don't worry Allah is your friend.

65
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
Don't worry Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam is your friend.

66
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.000
Don't worry the believers are your friends inshallah. May Allah comfort us as well.

67
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.000
If people have excommunicated you because you have now stood up for justice and the truth

68
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:39.000
don't worry you are heading in the right direction inshallah. May Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala grant us

69
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.000
companionship of Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam.

70
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Now you might have noticed as Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam

71
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:50.000
noticed that in this verse Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala says that those who establish salah

72
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.000
and give zakah whilst they are in ruku'ah. So Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wa sallam was wondering

73
00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:02.000
what is meant by this. As he walked out he saw a beggar. He was going towards his masjid and he saw a beggar.

74
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.000
And on one side he could see his masjid and he could see some of the companions who were standing in salah.

75
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.000
Some of them were in ruku'ah and so on.

76
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.000
So he asked this beggar because he knows that zakah is to do with giving. Has anyone given you anything today?

77
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:19.000
He said yes, I was given this ring. Who gave you this ring?

78
00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:25.000
So the beggar pointed at Ali ibn Abi Talib r.a. And Rasulullah sallallahu alaihi wa sallam

79
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.000
asked the beggar in what position of salah was he when he gave you the ring.

80
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.000
And the beggar said he was in ruku'ah. He took out his ring and gave it to me. Allahu Akbar!

81
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:40.000
So he gave the ring minutes, minutes before this and at that particular time

82
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.000
Jigreel was already there revealing the verses that your friend, Abdullah ibn sallam

83
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:51.000
is even Ali ibn Abi Talib r.a. Who happened to give zakah whilst he was in ruku'ah. Now some of us might ask,

84
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:57.000
is it allowed to give zakah whilst you are in ruku'ah? Let me inform you that at that time

85
00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:02.000
it was even allowed to speak a few words in salah. But when Allah revealed the verse

86
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.000
وَقُمُولِ اللَّهِ قَانِتِينَ

87
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:12.000
stand for the sake of Allah with total and utmost concentration. It became prohibited to speak.

88
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:18.000
It became prohibited to make unnecessary movements in salah. So up to today that is the ruling.

89
00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.000
But at that time it was still permissible. That is why Ali r.a. has been praised in the Quran

90
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.000
and he is regarded as a friend of Abdullah ibn sallam

91
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.000
and a friend of all those who have been oppressed in one way or another.

92
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.000
May Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala grant us the two understanding.

